an investment.

00:02:56.585 --> 00:02:58.887
Instead, what I tell you today,

00:02:58.887 --> 00:03:03.668
is that where your behavior will
matter most for the next 30 years.

00:03:03.668 --> 00:03:09.626
Is in your hands in the form of
the vote and civic engagement.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:20.353
Underrated, free, necessary and

00:03:20.353 --> 00:03:26.652
under tapped by the business community and
all of us.

00:03:30.029 --> 00:03:34.972
Before I go on, I want to confess
that I came to business school.

00:03:34.972 --> 00:03:37.263
Yes, Business School for

00:03:37.263 --> 00:03:42.796
the same reason as most of you to
take outsize bets on my career.

00:03:42.796 --> 00:03:47.048
I want to co found and
invest in amazing unicorns,

00:03:47.048 --> 00:03:51.623
build the best content
industry in the whole world.

00:03:51.623 --> 00:03:52.622
Thanks Stanford.

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:56.444
Maybe publish a book and really go big.

00:03:58.216 --> 00:04:02.866
But as I began achieving these goals.

00:04:02.866 --> 00:04:08.637
And I talked to over 100 companies in
the climate tech space in the past year.

00:04:08.637 --> 00:04:13.588
I couldn't help but notice an absence.

00:04:13.588 --> 00:04:18.807
You see, we are obsessed with becoming

00:04:18.807 --> 00:04:24.818
identifying the best
players on the field and

00:04:24.818 --> 00:04:27.996
I think that's great.

00:04:27.996 --> 00:04:33.037
But what will make the night and
day difference for

00:04:33.037 --> 00:04:37.000
our future is in fact, influencing and

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:44.822
electing the referees who are going to
change the much needed rules of the game.

00:04:44.822 --> 00:04:50.234
And I'm telling you, those rules have to
be changed in the fight against climate.

00:04:50.234 --> 00:04:55.430
In order to make the difference
between the future I described and

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:58.841
the one that you want
your children to see.

00:04:58.841 --> 00:05:02.658
I want to say that I too,
am a player on the field.

00:05:02.658 --> 00:05:05.829
I've been a player three
times starting at the GSB.

00:05:05.829 --> 00:05:07.543
And we haven't won a match yet.

00:05:07.543 --> 00:05:10.329
The first was when I met my classmates,

00:05:10.329 --> 00:05:13.884
Stella on Zoom before
starting business school.

00:05:13.884 --> 00:05:18.619
We were stoked by the idea of
creating the platform that will

00:05:18.619 --> 00:05:23.743
transform carbon emission tracking for
the food supply space.

00:05:23.743 --> 00:05:29.011
Now we somehow fooled some PhDs to
join us drank way too much coffee.

00:05:29.011 --> 00:05:32.091
And we were pitching to
some of the best VCs on

00:05:32.091 --> 00:05:35.769
Silicon Valley Sandhill Road
within three months.

00:05:35.769 --> 00:05:40.225
Wow, I was shocked but so excited.

00:05:40.225 --> 00:05:47.793
And said one VC Love your
passion love your idea.

00:05:47.793 --> 00:05:52.929
But this is rooted far too
heavily in the policy space,

00:05:52.929 --> 00:05:57.292
political incentives, standards setting.

00:05:57.292 --> 00:05:59.004
That's not where I put my money.

00:05:59.004 --> 00:06:01.012
I pass sorry.

00:06:01.012 --> 00:06:07.885
Me in my head you pass.

00:06:07.885 --> 00:06:09.235
Are you serious?

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:12.014
Will climate change not affect you too?

00:06:12.014 --> 00:06:16.724
If you don't find the solution, who will?

00:06:16.724 --> 00:06:20.883
This wake up call was extremely humbling.

00:06:20.883 --> 00:06:23.777
But it taught me two important things.

00:06:23.777 --> 00:06:28.720
One of course,
the investor had a right to 10x returns.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:30.342
That's their job.

00:06:30.342 --> 00:06:34.712
But more importantly, entrepreneurship and

00:06:34.712 --> 00:06:41.664
the private sector alone is not enough
to get us out of the climate crisis.

00:06:41.664 --> 00:06:43.540
Changing the rules is paramount.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:46.626
And I want to talk about how.

00:06:46.626 --> 00:06:50.284
In particular, what does it look like?

00:06:50.284 --> 00:06:56.314
And how does it involve you?

00:06:56.314 --> 00:06:59.351
I've lived in California for 10 years.

00:06:59.351 --> 00:07:05.387
One of the most consequential bills that
was passed is Senate Bill 100, in 2018.

00:07:08.463 --> 00:07:10.327
Who's going to charge their phone tonight?

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:16.632
Okay, looks like everybody.

00:07:16.632 --> 00:07:20.064
When you plug your phone
into that wall tonight,

00:07:20.064 --> 00:07:25.263
two thirds of the power which flows
into your device is from fossil fuels.

00:07:25.263 --> 00:07:29.621
The other third from renewables
in the state of California.

00:07:29.621 --> 00:07:33.702
If SB 100 is met by the 2050s,

00:07:33.702 --> 00:07:38.056
that two thirds is phased down to zero.

00:07:38.056 --> 00:07:41.378
By the time my kid goes to college.

00:07:41.378 --> 00:07:43.624
Why is this important?

00:07:43.624 --> 00:07:47.663
40% of our emissions come
from the power sector.

00:07:47.663 --> 00:07:53.063
So it's not about how many electric
cars we can produce or make or afford.

00:07:53.063 --> 00:07:56.798
If that grid is not clean if
those standards are not set.

00:07:56.798 --> 00:08:02.258
If SB 100 is not passed,
it doesn't make a difference.

00:08:02.258 --> 00:08:06.098
And it's not just about one
smart bill being passed.

00:08:06.098 --> 00:08:11.924
It was about the assembly member who
bravely put the bill on the floor,

00:08:11.924 --> 00:08:13.323
on your behalf.

00:08:13.323 --> 00:08:18.850
Lobbied and defended this bill
in all his drafts through

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:24.502
two years of lobbying from
over 300 external forces.

00:08:24.502 --> 00:08:29.308
That pressure test allowed your
voice to be heard on the floor and

00:08:29.308 --> 00:08:30.918
the bill was passed.

00:08:30.918 --> 00:08:36.034
The impact is huge,
because that decision inked

00:08:36.034 --> 00:08:41.535
in the law spurred 21 other
states to follow suit.

00:08:41.535 --> 00:08:44.916
And eventually the national
administration.

00:08:44.916 --> 00:08:51.025
2021 was a watershed
year in policy making.

00:08:51.025 --> 00:08:55.157
And I'm here to tell you it's
no coincidence that it was also

00:08:55.157 --> 00:08:57.264
the historically peak year for

00:08:57.264 --> 00:09:01.082
venture funding in the same
climate technology space.

00:09:04.045 --> 00:09:06.551
So that's how the rules are changed.

00:09:06.551 --> 00:09:07.731
And that's your role.

00:09:09.566 --> 00:09:11.615
Here is one more dimension.

00:09:11.615 --> 00:09:15.936
Raise your hand in the room
if you are approaching 30.

00:09:17.431 --> 00:09:20.742
Or remember what being 30 feels like.

00:09:22.868 --> 00:09:23.998
Thank you.

00:09:23.998 --> 00:09:30.735
Congratulations, because all of
you are the average lifespan

00:09:30.735 --> 00:09:36.341
of a coal fired plant or
an electric grid you choose.

00:09:36.341 --> 00:09:41.164
Now, think about the policymaker
who is sitting in their office,

00:09:41.164 --> 00:09:44.705
figuring out how to spend
their taxpayer money.

00:09:44.705 --> 00:09:50.438
On this one asset that has to have
a shelf life of 30 years into the future,

00:09:50.438 --> 00:09:57.012
critical infrastructure that will keep the
lights on for all of our future children.

00:09:57.012 --> 00:10:01.893
What a high stakes decision when
you only have one time to make

00:10:01.893 --> 00:10:06.114
it in this once in every
30 year purchasing cycle.

00:10:06.114 --> 00:10:11.159
Think about the ways that we can
de risk that decision by having

00:10:11.159 --> 00:10:16.507
the right incentives in place for
this particular policymaker.

00:10:16.507 --> 00:10:23.402
This is where you and
I all have a role in civic engagement.

00:10:23.402 --> 00:10:27.243
The best news is I know that you care.

00:10:27.243 --> 00:10:34.279
You want to act and therefore you have the
agency and the ability to create change.

00:10:37.235 --> 00:10:42.932
On that note, I tell you to vote
in all your elected officials

00:10:42.932 --> 00:10:48.981
who do have a plan for
changing the rules around climate change.

00:10:48.981 --> 00:10:55.570
Rules that do not show up in quarterly
earnings cycles or term sheets.

00:10:55.570 --> 00:11:00.763
These represent protection for
rural families who

00:11:00.763 --> 00:11:06.442
simply need their first
megawatt hour of electricity.

00:11:06.442 --> 00:11:11.498
These rules that don't show up in
term sheets include protection for

00:11:11.498 --> 00:11:13.161
entire communities.

00:11:13.161 --> 00:11:16.577
From Cape Town, in South Africa,
all the way to West Virginia.

00:11:16.577 --> 00:11:20.733
Here in the United States,
whose livelihoods are upended.

00:11:20.733 --> 00:11:22.877
When other interests force,

00:11:22.877 --> 00:11:27.342
the transition away from fossil
fuels in the next 30 years.

00:11:27.342 --> 00:11:31.335
When we think about your
political impact we must go beyond

00:11:31.335 --> 00:11:36.071
the presidential races to the state and
local in this conversation.

00:11:39.949 --> 00:11:43.561
I call you to become leaders
who make those hard choices.

00:11:43.561 --> 00:11:48.717
And I want to give you three
very concrete ways to do that as

00:11:48.717 --> 00:11:53.994
a player on the field, or
as a future referee of the game.

00:11:53.994 --> 00:11:57.906
Think about the five people that
you spend the most time with.

00:11:57.906 --> 00:12:06.098
Number one, research shows
that voting is a habitual act.

00:12:06.098 --> 00:12:09.594
It takes that parent or
that family member and

00:12:09.594 --> 00:12:12.818
friend to take a first timer to the booth.

00:12:12.818 --> 00:12:16.280
Can you take your family
to the next local election?

00:12:18.582 --> 00:12:20.722
Number two.

00:12:20.722 --> 00:12:25.558
Research also shows that loss
of social capital is the biggest

00:12:25.558 --> 00:12:30.593
inhibitor to voices that want to
speak out in a homogenous group.

00:12:30.593 --> 00:12:35.445
In this case, think about the climate
skeptic and your investment team.

00:12:35.445 --> 00:12:39.631
Or think about that voice
who want to drive change but

00:12:39.631 --> 00:12:42.170
finds no ally in a silent room.

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:45.109
Can you be that ally?

00:12:45.109 --> 00:12:49.153
Or that disruptor of a social norm?

00:12:52.296 --> 00:12:57.861
Okay and then number three for those
of you sitting here who want to run for

00:12:57.861 --> 00:13:01.027
office one day and I would love to see it.

00:13:01.027 --> 00:13:07.199
You can engage with a Stanford funded
nonprofit called climate cabinet.

00:13:07.199 --> 00:13:10.431
Whose whole job is to empower you and

00:13:10.431 --> 00:13:15.175
your staffers with a knowledgeable,
actionable,

00:13:15.175 --> 00:13:20.804
relevant and constituent
friendly platform about climate.

00:13:20.804 --> 00:13:26.697
From how we produce power to how we
grow our food to how we manufacture.

00:13:26.697 --> 00:13:29.748
And run our buildings.

00:13:29.748 --> 00:13:33.586
The possibilities are there.

00:13:33.586 --> 00:13:36.834
And I can feel it in all of your hands.

00:13:36.834 --> 00:13:40.898
So let's come back to the 2050
that I had talked about.

00:13:40.898 --> 00:13:44.843
Actually not the one I had talked about,
but

00:13:44.843 --> 00:13:48.794
the one that we all want
our children to see.

00:13:48.794 --> 00:13:50.863
What do you want them to see?

00:13:50.863 --> 00:13:55.587
Will it be blue skies or orange?

00:13:55.587 --> 00:14:01.740
What is the air that they
smell when they play soccer or

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:07.368
the water that they taste
at the end of a long day.

00:14:10.107 --> 00:14:15.286
I know that each of us all have
an important role to play.

00:14:15.286 --> 00:14:20.439
And from this day forward,
we will be judged on

00:14:20.439 --> 00:14:27.853
the decisions we make when it mattered or
the decisions we did not.

00:14:27.853 --> 00:14:32.841
Together, we can all employ
civic engagement and

00:14:32.841 --> 00:14:39.860
our votes to move the needle forward for
the future that we want to see.

00:14:39.860 --> 00:14:41.226
Thank you.

00:14:41.226 --> 00:14:42.521
